From: MatonOS
Subject: [PATCH] module-raop-sink: include openssl/bn.h explicitly

The sink calls BN_bin2bn/BN_free but relies on OpenSSL including bn.h
through rsa.h. BoringSSL does not, so the build fails there.
---
diff --git a/src/modules/module-raop-sink.c b/src/modules/module-raop-sink.c
index 36fdfa04d..89278ea95 100644
--- a/src/modules/module-raop-sink.c
+++ b/src/modules/module-raop-sink.c
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@
 #endif
 #include <openssl/rand.h>
 #include <openssl/rsa.h>
+#include <openssl/bn.h>
 #include <openssl/aes.h>
 #include <openssl/md5.h>
 #include <openssl/evp.h>
